      "connectsTo": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/34546779",
      "details": "<p>Two locations have been tentatively suggested for Kundu (classical\u00a0Kyinda): (1) modern <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/658378\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Anavarza</a>, ca. twenty km southeast of Kozan (=\u00a0Siss\u00fb), and (2) modern Tirmil Tepe, ca. two km northeast of <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/648555\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Mersin</a>. The former seems more plausible given\u00a0that Kundu and Siss\u00fb mentioned together in Esarhaddon's inscriptions, although this cannot be proven with certainty. Note that <span>Anavarza is generally associated with classical\u00a0<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/658378\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Anazarbos/Caesarea/Ioustin(ian)oupolis</a>.\u00a0</span>Kundu is not in the vicinity of <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/678393\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Sidon</a>, as suggested by W. Mayer in 1995.\u00a0</p>",
